.TH CHTTPSVR_ROUTER_ON_STREAM 3 "2026-08-03" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpsvr_router_on_stream \- register a streaming handler on a sub-router
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttpserver.h>

ccol_retval_t chttpsvr_router_on_stream(chttpsvr_router *router,
                                         chttp_method_t method,
                                         const char *pattern,
                                         chttpsvr_handler_fn fn,
                                         void *ctx);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This function works like chttpsvr_register_streaming_handler, but it
registers the route on a sub-router.  Every rule that
chttpsvr_register_streaming_handler gives for a pattern applies here
too.  pattern must start with '/'.  A {name} segment must hold only
[A-Za-z0-9_].  The same {name} must not appear more than once.  This
function also supports CHTTP_ANY as the method argument.  The handler
runs on the streaming pool of the server, exactly as a handler of
chttpsvr_register_streaming_handler does.

This function first checks that nothing destroyed the server that owns
router.  That check also covers a concurrent destroy from another
thread.  A call that races a chttpsvr_destroy of the owning server
returns ccol_invalid_args, and touches no freed memory.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success on success.
ccol_invalid_args when router, pattern or fn is NULL; when pattern
                  does not start with '/'; when pattern has two
                  slashes together or a slash at the end; when a
                  {name} segment has a character outside
                  [A-Za-z0-9_]; when the same {name} appears more than
                  once; or when something destroyed the server that
                  owns router.
ccol_not_enough_memory when an allocation fails.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpsvr_register_streaming_handler (3),
.BR chttpsvr_subrouter (3)
